field. We derive a symmetric, nonrecursive Grassmann-type formula for the
dimension of their sum. The formula expresses the total dimension loss through
intersections of a distinguished subspace with partial sums of the remaining
subspaces, with coefficients determined by the number of subspaces involved. We
also show that the formula admits a Shapley-value interpretation for the
associated representable polymatroid. Grouping the correction terms by the
number of participating subspaces yields a nonnegative dimension-defect
